 ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (a+b)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $A+B$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B),$ the column space of $A+B.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(A+B).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/02/02a739d8888f2b46b81075218693e6b2cc87e3c5b81b522abfc9246dcd7c870d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186397956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186397955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397951 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4f937f66-6317-5bbf-a1a5-7a91aa314279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397952 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{Null}(A+B)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397952 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397952 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4a3e2b6-7b29-5528-96b5-7573a1aadd7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397953 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397953 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186397953 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4bbf2858-8656-5cf8-89b6-f411004b18f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [